Ladybird now lays out an in-flow flex or grid item with align-self or
justify-self set to anchor-center exactly as with center. Blink does the
same: Its ResolvedSelfAlignment() turns anchor-center into center for a
box with no anchor-center offset, and its AxisEdgeFromItemPosition()
gives a grid item’s kAnchorCenter the center edge. In WebKit, the
columnAxisPositionForGridItem() and rowAxisPositionForGridItem() of
RenderGrid map AnchorCenter to GridAxisCenter, and FlexFormattingUtils::
alignmentOffset() gives AnchorCenter the same offset as Center. In
Gecko, EnterAlignPackingSpace() aligns a flex item with ANCHOR_CENTER as
CENTER, and CSSAlignUtils::AlignJustifySelf() also treats ANCHOR_CENTER
with no anchor as CENTER.
